/-!
# The affine chart of Stacks tag 063W

`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ChartInput063W` is the one statement on which the whole of the
"equality_flat" clause of Stacks tag 063W was left resting:  under the hypotheses of that clause,
every open neighbourhood of the point contains an affine open over which the ideal of the closed
subscheme is generated by a family of sections weakly regular in the ring of sections.  This file
proves it, and therefore proves `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Statement063W`.

No new mathematics is involved:  the fibre hypothesis has already been turned into
ring-theoretic data in the local ring at the point
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.exists_mem_stalkIdeal_isRegular_quotient`), and the two spreading-out
theorems that consume that data are already in the tree
(`Stacks.RingTheory.SpreadingOut.exists_notMem_isWeaklyRegular_and_flat_quotient_away`, Stacks
062Y (3), and `Stacks.RingTheory.SpreadingOut.exists_notMem_map_eq_map_away`, Stacks 046Y).  What
is done here is to choose the chart and match the two up.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.stalkMap_hom_comp_germ`: the stalk map of a morphism composed with a
  germ of the base is a germ of the source composed with a map of sections.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ideal_le_primeIdealOf`: the ideal of a closed subscheme over an affine
  open is contained in the prime of any of its points.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.flat_quotient_stalkIdeal`: the quotient of a local ring by the ideal
  cut out by a closed subscheme flat over the base is flat over the base.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.exists_affineOpen_isWeaklyRegular_ideal_of_fibre`: the affine chart.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.chartInput063W`: `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ChartInput063W`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.statement063W`: `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Statement063W`.

## Implementation notes

The chart is an affine open `W` of the base around the image of the point, and an affine open `U`
of the source inside the prescribed neighbourhood and over `W`;  `A = Γ(S, W)`, `B = Γ(X, U)`,
the prime `q` of `B` is the one of the point, and the ideal is `T.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩` — working with
the ideal of the ideal sheaf data rather than with the kernel of a section map saves the whole
comparison that `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/MoreMorphisms/RelativeRegularImmersion/Gluing.lean`
has to make.

Three dictionary entries connect the local ring `𝒪_{X, x}` to the ring `B`:  it is an abstract
localization of `B` at `q` (`AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.isLocalization_stalk`), the ideal cut
out in it is the extension of `T.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩`
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.stalkIdeal_eq_map_germ`), and the prime of `A` below `q` is the one of
the image point (`AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.comap_primeIdealOf_appLE`).  The passage from
`𝒪_{X, x}` to `Localization.AtPrime q`, which is what the spreading out is stated for, is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.exists_mem_isRegular_fibre_atPrime`.

Flatness of `T` over `S` at the point is used in the single shape the spreading out needs, namely
flatness of `𝒪_{X, x}` modulo the ideal cut out:  that quotient is the local ring of `T` at the
point, which is flat over the local ring of `S`, which is flat over `A`.

The two elements produced by the two spreading-out theorems are different, so the chart is the
intersection of their basic opens, written as a basic open of the first;  weak regularity survives
the second shrinking because sections of a basic open are a localization
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isWeaklyRegular_res_basicOpen_of_away`) and the ideal equality survives
it because an ideal sheaf is quasi-coherent
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.map_ideal`).

Every step that mentions the point `⟨x, hx⟩` of `T.subscheme` is assembled with `exact` and
`congrArg` rather than with `rw`:  the underlying space of `T.subscheme` reduces to `T.support`
only at default transparency, so a rewrite in such a goal is rejected as not type-correct.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.22.8 (Tag 063W)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063W)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 062Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/062Y)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 046Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/046Y)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Opposite TopologicalSpace AlgebraicGeometry RingTheory.Sequence
open Stacks.RingTheory.SpreadingOut
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

variable {X S : Scheme.{u}}

/-! ### Dictionary entries -/

/-- **The stalk map of a morphism, read on sections.**  For affine opens `x ∈ U ⊆ f⁻¹W` the germ
at `f x` followed by the stalk map of `f` at `x` is the map of sections `Γ(S, W) → Γ(X, U)`
followed by the germ at `x`. -/
theorem stalkMap_hom_comp_germ (f : X ⟶ S) {x : X} {W : S.Opens} {U : X.Opens}
    (hUW : U ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ W) (hxU : x ∈ U) (hxW : f x ∈ W) :
    (f.stalkMap x).hom.comp (S.presheaf.germ W (f x) hxW).hom
      = (X.presheaf.germ U x hxU).hom.comp (f.appLE W U hUW).hom := by
  rw [← CommRingCat.hom_comp, ← CommRingCat.hom_comp, f.germ_stalkMap W x hxW]
  congr 1
  rw [Scheme.Hom.appLE]
  simp

/-- A section over an affine open outside the prime of a point has invertible germ there. -/
private theorem isUnit_germ_of_notMem_primeIdealOf {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {x : X}
    (hxU : x ∈ U) {s : Γ(X, U)} (hs : s ∉ (hU.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : ↥U)).asIdeal) :
    IsUnit ((X.presheaf.germ U x hxU).hom s) := by
  let _ : Algebra Γ(X, U) (X.presheaf.stalk x) := X.presheaf.algebra_section_stalk ⟨x, hxU⟩
  have _ : IsLocalization.AtPrime (X.presheaf.stalk x)
      (hU.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : ↥U)).asIdeal := hU.isLocalization_stalk ⟨x, hxU⟩
  exact (IsLocalization.AtPrime.isUnit_to_map_iff _
    (hU.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : ↥U)).asIdeal s).mpr hs

/-- **The ideal of a closed subscheme lies in the prime of each of its points.**  If it did not,
a section of it would be invertible in the local ring, and the ideal it cuts out there would be
the whole local ring, which it is not. -/
theorem ideal_le_primeIdealOf (T : X.IdealSheafData) {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {x : X}
    (hxU : x ∈ U) (hx : x ∈ T.support) :
    T.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩ ≤ (hU.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : ↥U)).asIdeal := by
  intro s hs
  by_contra hsq
  exact stalkIdeal_ne_top T x hx (Ideal.eq_top_of_isUnit_mem _
    ((stalkIdeal_eq_map_germ T x hx hU hxU).ge (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hs))
    (isUnit_germ_of_notMem_primeIdealOf hU hxU hsq))

/-- **Flatness of the local ring of a closed subscheme, read on the ambient local ring.**  If the
closed subscheme `T` of `X` is flat over `S` at a point `x`, then the quotient of `𝒪_{X, x}` by
the ideal that `T` cuts out there is flat over the sections of `S` over an affine open containing
the image of `x`.

That quotient is the local ring of `T` at `x`, which is flat over `𝒪_{S, f x}` by hypothesis,
and `𝒪_{S, f x}` is a localization of `Γ(S, W)`. -/
theorem flat_quotient_stalkIdeal (f : X ⟶ S) (T : X.IdealSheafData) (x : X) (hx : x ∈ T.support)
    (hflat : ((T.subschemeι ≫ f).stalkMap (⟨x, hx⟩ : T.subscheme)).hom.Flat)
    {W : S.Opens} (hW : IsAffineOpen W) (hxW : f x ∈ W)
    [Algebra Γ(S, W) (X.presheaf.stalk x)]
    (halg : ∀ t : Γ(S, W), algebraMap Γ(S, W) (X.presheaf.stalk x) t
      = (f.stalkMap x).hom ((S.presheaf.germ W (f x) hxW).hom t)) :
    Module.Flat Γ(S, W) (X.presheaf.stalk x ⧸ stalkIdeal T x hx) := by
  have hcomp : (T.subschemeι ≫ f).stalkMap (⟨x, hx⟩ : T.subscheme)
      = f.stalkMap x ≫ T.subschemeι.stalkMap (⟨x, hx⟩ : T.subscheme) :=
    Scheme.Hom.stalkMap_comp T.subschemeι f (⟨x, hx⟩ : T.subscheme)
  let _ : Algebra Γ(S, W) (S.presheaf.stalk (f x)) :=
    S.presheaf.algebra_section_stalk ⟨f x, hxW⟩
  have _ : IsLocalization.AtPrime (S.presheaf.stalk (f x))
      (hW.primeIdealOf (⟨f x, hxW⟩ : ↥W)).asIdeal := hW.isLocalization_stalk ⟨f x, hxW⟩
  have _ : Module.Flat Γ(S, W) (S.presheaf.stalk (f x)) :=
    IsLocalization.flat _ (hW.primeIdealOf (⟨f x, hxW⟩ : ↥W)).asIdeal.primeCompl
  let _ : Algebra (S.presheaf.stalk (f x)) (T.subscheme.presheaf.stalk (⟨x, hx⟩ : T.subscheme)) :=
    ((T.subschemeι ≫ f).stalkMap (⟨x, hx⟩ : T.subscheme)).hom.toAlgebra
  have _ : Module.Flat (S.presheaf.stalk (f x))
      (T.subscheme.presheaf.stalk (⟨x, hx⟩ : T.subscheme)) := hflat
  let _ : Algebra Γ(S, W) (T.subscheme.presheaf.stalk (⟨x, hx⟩ : T.subscheme)) :=
    ((T.subschemeι.stalkMap (⟨x, hx⟩ : T.subscheme)).hom.comp
      (algebraMap Γ(S, W) (X.presheaf.stalk x))).toAlgebra
  have _ : IsScalarTower Γ(S, W) (S.presheaf.stalk (f x))
      (T.subscheme.presheaf.stalk (⟨x, hx⟩ : T.subscheme)) := by
    refine .of_algebraMap_eq fun t => ?_
    refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun z : X.presheaf.stalk x =>
      (T.subschemeι.stalkMap (⟨x, hx⟩ : T.subscheme)).hom z) (halg t)) ?_
    exact (congrArg (fun θ : S.presheaf.stalk (f x) ⟶
        T.subscheme.presheaf.stalk (⟨x, hx⟩ : T.subscheme) =>
      θ.hom ((S.presheaf.germ W (f x) hxW).hom t)) hcomp).symm
  have _ := Module.Flat.trans Γ(S, W) (S.presheaf.stalk (f x))
    (T.subscheme.presheaf.stalk (⟨x, hx⟩ : T.subscheme))
  let e : (X.presheaf.stalk x ⧸ stalkIdeal T x hx) ≃+*
      T.subscheme.presheaf.stalk (⟨x, hx⟩ : T.subscheme) :=
    RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective
      (T.subschemeι.stalkMap_surjective (⟨x, hx⟩ : T.subscheme))
  exact Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv (AlgEquiv.ofRingEquiv (f := e) fun _ => rfl).toLinearEquiv

/-! ### Shrinking the chart -/

/-- Extending an ideal along two successive restriction maps extends it along their composite. -/
theorem map_res_res {U V' V : X.Opens} (h₁ : V' ≤ U) (h₂ : V ≤ V') (h : V ≤ U)
    (K : Ideal Γ(X, U)) :
    (K.map (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h₁).op).hom).map (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h₂).op).hom
      = K.map (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op).hom := by
  rw [Ideal.map_map, ← CommRingCat.hom_comp, ← X.presheaf.map_comp]
  rfl

/-- **Weak regularity passes to a basic open.**  The ring of sections of a basic open of an affine
open is a localization of the ring of sections, and weak regularity of a sequence is preserved by
localization. -/
theorem isWeaklyRegular_res_basicOpen {V U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (t : Γ(X, U))
    (hV : V = X.basicOpen t) (hVU : V ≤ U) {r : ℕ} (c : Fin r → Γ(X, U))
    (h : IsWeaklyRegular Γ(X, U) (List.ofFn c)) :
    IsWeaklyRegular Γ(X, V) (List.ofFn fun k => X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op (c k)) := by
  subst hV
  have _ := hU.isLocalization_basicOpen t
  have h' := h.of_isLocalization Γ(X, X.basicOpen t) (Submonoid.powers t)
  rwa [List.map_ofFn] at h'

/-- **An ideal equality in the localization away from a section holds on the basic open.**  The
sections over a basic open of an affine open are a localization away from the section, so an
equality of extended ideals there is an equality of the ideals they extend to on the basic
open. -/
theorem map_res_basicOpen_eq_of_away {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (g : Γ(X, U))
    (J I : Ideal Γ(X, U))
    (h : I.map (algebraMap Γ(X, U) (Localization.Away g))
      = J.map (algebraMap Γ(X, U) (Localization.Away g))) :
    I.map (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)).op).hom
      = J.map (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)).op).hom := by
  have _ := hU.isLocalization_basicOpen g
  set e := IsLocalization.algEquiv (Submonoid.powers g) (Localization.Away g)
    Γ(X, X.basicOpen g)
  have hcomp : ((e : Localization.Away g →+* Γ(X, X.basicOpen g))).comp
      (algebraMap Γ(X, U) (Localization.Away g))
      = algebraMap Γ(X, U) Γ(X, X.basicOpen g) := RingHom.ext e.commutes
  have hmapped := congrArg
    (Ideal.map (e : Localization.Away g →+* Γ(X, X.basicOpen g))) h
  rwa [Ideal.map_map, Ideal.map_map, hcomp.trans (RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra _)] at hmapped

/-- **The fibre ideal at a point, read on an affine chart.**  For affine opens `x ∈ U ⊆ f⁻¹W`, the
maximal ideal of `𝒪_{S, f x}` extends to the extension of the prime of `Γ(S, W)` below the prime
of `x` in `Γ(X, U)`. -/
private theorem map_maximalIdeal_stalk_eq_map_comap_primeIdealOf (f : X ⟶ S) {x : X} {W : S.Opens}
    {U : X.Opens} (hW : IsAffineOpen W) (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hUW : U ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ W) (hxU : x ∈ U)
    (hxW : f x ∈ W) :
    Ideal.map (f.stalkMap x).hom (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (S.presheaf.stalk (f x)))
      = ((hU.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : ↥U)).asIdeal.comap (f.appLE W U hUW).hom).map
          ((X.presheaf.germ U x hxU).hom.comp (f.appLE W U hUW).hom) := by
  let _ : Algebra Γ(S, W) (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
    ((X.presheaf.germ U x hxU).hom.comp (f.appLE W U hUW).hom).toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra Γ(S, W) (S.presheaf.stalk (f x)) :=
    S.presheaf.algebra_section_stalk ⟨f x, hxW⟩
  have _ : IsLocalization.AtPrime (S.presheaf.stalk (f x))
      (hW.primeIdealOf (⟨f x, hxW⟩ : ↥W)).asIdeal := hW.isLocalization_stalk ⟨f x, hxW⟩
  have _ : (hW.primeIdealOf (⟨f x, hxW⟩ : ↥W)).asIdeal.IsPrime :=
    (hW.primeIdealOf (⟨f x, hxW⟩ : ↥W)).isPrime
  let _ : Algebra (S.presheaf.stalk (f x)) (X.presheaf.stalk x) := (f.stalkMap x).hom.toAlgebra
  have _ : IsScalarTower Γ(S, W) (S.presheaf.stalk (f x)) (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
    .of_algebraMap_eq fun t => (RingHom.congr_fun (stalkMap_hom_comp_germ f hUW hxU hxW) t).symm
  have hcomap : (hU.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : ↥U)).asIdeal.comap (f.appLE W U hUW).hom
      = (hW.primeIdealOf (⟨f x, hxW⟩ : ↥W)).asIdeal :=
    congrArg PrimeSpectrum.asIdeal (IsAffineOpen.comap_primeIdealOf_appLE W hW U hU hUW hxU)
  rw [hcomap]
  exact map_maximalIdeal_eq_map_of_isLocalization _

/-! ### The affine chart -/

/-- **The algebraic core of the affine chart of Stacks tag 063W.**  On affine opens
`x ∈ U ⊆ f⁻¹W`, Stacks 062Y (3) and Stacks 046Y produce a family `c` of sections over `U` and two
sections `g₁, g₂` outside the prime of `x`, such that `c` is weakly regular away from `g₁` and
generates the ideal of `T` away from `g₂`. -/
private theorem exists_notMem_isWeaklyRegular_and_ideal_eq_away (f : X ⟶ S) [Flat f]
    [LocallyOfFinitePresentation f] (T : X.IdealSheafData)
    [LocallyOfFinitePresentation T.subschemeι] (x : X) (hx : x ∈ T.support)
    (hfib : ∃ V : (f.fiber (f x)).Opens, f.asFiber x ∈ V ∧ IsQuasiRegularImmersion
      (((T.comap (f.fiberι (f x))).comap V.ι).subschemeι))
    (hflat : ((T.subschemeι ≫ f).stalkMap (⟨x, hx⟩ : T.subscheme)).hom.Flat)
    {W : S.Opens} {U : X.Opens} (hW : IsAffineOpen W) (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hUW : U ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ W)
    (hxU : x ∈ U) (hxW : f x ∈ W) :
    ∃ (r : ℕ) (c : Fin r → Γ(X, U)) (g₁ g₂ : Γ(X, U)),
      g₁ ∉ (hU.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : ↥U)).asIdeal ∧
      g₂ ∉ (hU.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : ↥U)).asIdeal ∧
      IsWeaklyRegular (Localization.Away g₁)
        (List.ofFn fun k => algebraMap Γ(X, U) (Localization.Away g₁) (c k)) ∧
      (T.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩).map (algebraMap Γ(X, U) (Localization.Away g₂))
        = (Ideal.span (Set.range c)).map (algebraMap Γ(X, U) (Localization.Away g₂)) := by
  classical
  -- the two rings, and the prime of the point
  let _ : Algebra Γ(S, W) Γ(X, U) := (f.appLE W U hUW).hom.toAlgebra
  have _ : Module.Flat Γ(S, W) Γ(X, U) := f.flat_appLE hW hU hUW
  have _ : Algebra.FinitePresentation Γ(S, W) Γ(X, U) := f.finitePresentation_appLE hW hU hUW
  have _ : (hU.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : ↥U)).asIdeal.IsPrime :=
    (hU.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : ↥U)).isPrime
  -- the local ring at the point, as an abstract localization of `Γ(X, U)`
  let _ : Algebra Γ(X, U) (X.presheaf.stalk x) := X.presheaf.algebra_section_stalk ⟨x, hxU⟩
  have _ : IsLocalization.AtPrime (X.presheaf.stalk x)
      (hU.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : ↥U)).asIdeal := hU.isLocalization_stalk ⟨x, hxU⟩
  let _ : Algebra Γ(S, W) (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
    ((X.presheaf.germ U x hxU).hom.comp (f.appLE W U hUW).hom).toAlgebra
  have _ : IsScalarTower Γ(S, W) Γ(X, U) (X.presheaf.stalk x) := .of_algebraMap_eq fun _ => rfl
  have halg : ∀ t : Γ(S, W), algebraMap Γ(S, W) (X.presheaf.stalk x) t
      = (f.stalkMap x).hom ((S.presheaf.germ W (f x) hxW).hom t) := fun t =>
    (RingHom.congr_fun (stalkMap_hom_comp_germ f hUW hxU hxW) t).symm
  -- the ideal cutting out the fibre, as the extension of the prime below the point
  have hP : Ideal.map (f.stalkMap x).hom
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (S.presheaf.stalk (f x)))
      = ((hU.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : ↥U)).asIdeal.comap
          (algebraMap Γ(S, W) Γ(X, U))).map (algebraMap Γ(S, W) (X.presheaf.stalk x)) :=
    map_maximalIdeal_stalk_eq_map_comap_primeIdealOf f hW hU hUW hxU hxW
  -- the ideal of `T` on the chart, and the ideal it cuts out in the local ring
  have hstalk : stalkIdeal T x hx
      = (T.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩).map (algebraMap Γ(X, U) (X.presheaf.stalk x)) :=
    stalkIdeal_eq_map_germ T x hx hU hxU
  have hIq : T.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩ ≤ (hU.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : ↥U)).asIdeal :=
    ideal_le_primeIdealOf T hU hxU hx
  have hIfg : (T.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩).FG :=
    (Stacks.Flatness.locallyOfFinitePresentation_subschemeι_iff T).mp inferInstance ⟨U, hU⟩
  -- the fibre dictionary, moved to the concrete localization at the prime
  obtain ⟨r, d, hd, hregd, hled⟩ := exists_mem_stalkIdeal_isRegular_quotient f T x hx hfib
  obtain ⟨c, hcI, hcreg, hcle, -⟩ := exists_mem_isRegular_fibre_atPrime
    (hU.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : ↥U)).asIdeal (T.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩) d _ hP
    (fun i => hstalk.le (hd i)) hregd (hstalk.ge.trans hled)
  -- flatness of the quotient at the prime
  have _ := flat_quotient_stalkIdeal f T x hx hflat hW hxW halg
  have hIflat := flat_quotient_map_atPrime_of_abstract (A := Γ(S, W))
    (O := X.presheaf.stalk x) (hU.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : ↥U)).asIdeal (T.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩)
    (Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq Γ(S, W) hstalk).symm.toLinearEquiv)
  -- Stacks 062Y (3) and Stacks 046Y
  obtain ⟨g₁, hg₁, hwr, -⟩ := exists_notMem_isWeaklyRegular_and_flat_quotient_away
    (A := Γ(S, W)) (hU.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : ↥U)).asIdeal c (fun i => hIq (hcI i)) hcreg
  obtain ⟨g₂, hg₂, heq⟩ := exists_notMem_map_eq_map_away (A := Γ(S, W))
    (hU.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : ↥U)).asIdeal (Ideal.span (Set.range c)) (T.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩)
    (Ideal.span_le.mpr (Set.range_subset_iff.mpr hcI))
    (Submodule.fg_span (Set.finite_range c)) hIfg hIflat hcle
  exact ⟨r, c, g₁, g₂, hg₁, hg₂, hwr, heq⟩

/-- **Shrinking the chart to `D(g₁) ∩ D(g₂)`.**  If a family `c` of sections over an affine open
`U` is weakly regular away from `g₁` and generates the ideal of `T` away from `g₂`, then on
`D(g₁) ∩ D(g₂)` the restrictions of `c` are weakly regular and generate the ideal of `T`. -/
private theorem exists_basicOpen_isWeaklyRegular_ideal_of_away (T : X.IdealSheafData) {U : X.Opens}
    (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {x : X} {r : ℕ} (c : Fin r → Γ(X, U)) {g₁ g₂ : Γ(X, U)}
    (hx₁ : x ∈ X.basicOpen g₁) (hx₂ : x ∈ X.basicOpen g₂)
    (hwr : IsWeaklyRegular (Localization.Away g₁)
      (List.ofFn fun k => algebraMap Γ(X, U) (Localization.Away g₁) (c k)))
    (heq : (T.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩).map (algebraMap Γ(X, U) (Localization.Away g₂))
      = (Ideal.span (Set.range c)).map (algebraMap Γ(X, U) (Localization.Away g₂))) :
    ∃ (V : X.Opens) (hV : IsAffineOpen V), x ∈ V ∧ V ≤ U ∧
      ∃ c' : Fin r → Γ(X, V), T.ideal ⟨V, hV⟩ = Ideal.span (Set.range c') ∧
        IsWeaklyRegular Γ(X, V) (List.ofFn c') := by
  -- the chart `D(g₁) ∩ D(g₂)`, written as a basic open of `D(g₁)`
  have hV₁ : IsAffineOpen (X.basicOpen g₁) := hU.basicOpen g₁
  have hV₁U : X.basicOpen g₁ ≤ U := X.basicOpen_le g₁
  set t : Γ(X, X.basicOpen g₁) := X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hV₁U).op g₂
  have hV : IsAffineOpen (X.basicOpen t) := hV₁.basicOpen t
  have hVV₁ : X.basicOpen t ≤ X.basicOpen g₁ := X.basicOpen_le t
  have hVU : X.basicOpen t ≤ U := hVV₁.trans hV₁U
  have hVbo : X.basicOpen t = X.basicOpen g₁ ⊓ X.basicOpen g₂ :=
    X.basicOpen_res g₂ (homOfLE hV₁U).op
  have hVV₂ : X.basicOpen t ≤ X.basicOpen g₂ := hVbo.le.trans inf_le_right
  refine ⟨X.basicOpen t, hV, hVbo ▸ ⟨hx₁, hx₂⟩, hVU,
    fun k => X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op (c k), ?_, ?_⟩
  · -- the ideal equality, restricted from `D(g₂)`
    have hres : (T.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩).map (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op).hom
        = Ideal.span (Set.range fun k => X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op (c k)) := by
      rw [← map_res_res (X.basicOpen_le g₂) hVV₂ hVU, map_res_basicOpen_eq_of_away hU g₂ _ _ heq,
        map_res_res (X.basicOpen_le g₂) hVV₂ hVU, Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
      rfl
    exact (T.map_ideal (U := ⟨X.basicOpen t, hV⟩) (V := ⟨U, hU⟩) hVU).symm.trans hres
  · -- weak regularity, restricted from `D(g₁)`
    have hwr₁ := isWeaklyRegular_res_basicOpen_of_away hU g₁ c hwr
    have hwr₂ := isWeaklyRegular_res_basicOpen hV₁ t rfl hVV₁
      (fun k => X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hV₁U).op (c k)) hwr₁
    have hres : ∀ k, X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVV₁).op
        (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hV₁U).op (c k))
        = X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op (c k) := by
      intro k
      rw [← CommRingCat.comp_apply, ← X.presheaf.map_comp]
      rfl
    simpa only [hres] using hwr₂

/-- **The affine chart of Stacks tag 063W.**  Let `f : X ⟶ S` be flat and locally of finite
presentation, let `T` be a closed subscheme of `X` locally of finite presentation over `X`, and
let `x` be a point of `T` over which `T` cuts out a quasi-regular immersion on the fibre and at
which `T` is flat over `S`.  Then every open neighbourhood of `x` contains an affine open over
which the ideal of `T` is generated by a family of sections weakly regular in the ring of
sections.

The family comes from the fibre at `x` by `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry`'s fibre dictionary, and the
affine open is the intersection of the two basic opens produced by Stacks 062Y (3) and
Stacks 046Y. -/
theorem exists_affineOpen_isWeaklyRegular_ideal_of_fibre (f : X ⟶ S) [Flat f]
    [LocallyOfFinitePresentation f] (T : X.IdealSheafData)
    [LocallyOfFinitePresentation T.subschemeι] (x : X) (hx : x ∈ T.support)
    (hfib : ∃ V : (f.fiber (f x)).Opens, f.asFiber x ∈ V ∧ IsQuasiRegularImmersion
      (((T.comap (f.fiberι (f x))).comap V.ι).subschemeι))
    (hflat : ((T.subschemeι ≫ f).stalkMap (⟨x, hx⟩ : T.subscheme)).hom.Flat)
    (V₀ : X.Opens) (hxV₀ : x ∈ V₀) :
    ∃ (V : X.Opens) (hV : IsAffineOpen V), x ∈ V ∧ V ≤ V₀ ∧
      ∃ (r : ℕ) (c : Fin r → Γ(X, V)), T.ideal ⟨V, hV⟩ = Ideal.span (Set.range c) ∧
        IsWeaklyRegular Γ(X, V) (List.ofFn c) := by
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hxW, -⟩ := Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp S.isBasis_affineOpens
    (show f x ∈ (⊤ : S.Opens) from trivial)
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hxU, hUle⟩ := Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp X.isBasis_affineOpens
    (show x ∈ V₀ ⊓ f ⁻¹ᵁ W from ⟨hxV₀, hxW⟩)
  obtain ⟨r, c, g₁, g₂, hg₁, hg₂, hwr, heq⟩ := exists_notMem_isWeaklyRegular_and_ideal_eq_away
    f T x hx hfib hflat hW hU (fun _ h => (hUle h).2) hxU hxW
  -- a section outside the prime is invertible at the point
  have hmem : ∀ s : Γ(X, U), s ∉ (hU.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : ↥U)).asIdeal →
      x ∈ X.basicOpen s := fun s hs =>
    (X.mem_basicOpen s x hxU).mpr (isUnit_germ_of_notMem_primeIdealOf hU hxU hs)
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hxV, hVU, c', hc', hreg⟩ := exists_basicOpen_isWeaklyRegular_ideal_of_away T hU c
    (hmem g₁ hg₁) (hmem g₂ hg₂) hwr heq
  exact ⟨V, hV, hxV, fun _ h => (hUle (hVU h)).1, r, c', hc', hreg⟩

/-- **The affine-chart input of Stacks tag 063W.** -/
theorem chartInput063W : ChartInput063W.{u} := by
  intro X S f hf hfp T hT x hx hfib hflat V₀ hxV₀
  exact exists_affineOpen_isWeaklyRegular_ideal_of_fibre f T x hx hfib hflat V₀ hxV₀

/-- **The "equality_flat" clause of Stacks tag 063W.**  Near a point of a closed subscheme which
is flat over the base and cuts out a quasi-regular immersion on the fibre, the subscheme is a
relative quasi-regular immersion over the base and a regular immersion. -/
theorem statement063W : Statement063W.{u} :=
  statement063W_of_chartInput063W chartInput063W

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry

